  "task_text": " Review\n6/4 XP\nPeriodic Functions\nCompleted @ 12:18 PM\nPREREQUISITES\n Piecewise Functions\n1.Drawing the Graph of a Periodic Function\n?\n\nPart of the graph of a function \n𝑦\n=\n𝑓\n(\n𝑥\n)\n with period \n2\n is shown above. What is the graph of \n𝑦\n=\n𝑓\n(\n𝑥\n)\n on the interval \n−\n4\n≤\n𝑥\n≤\n4\n?\n\nETue, Jul 29th @ 12:16 PM|Elapsed: 0:35\nCorrect\n2.Identifying the Period of a Function Given Its Graph\n?\n\nWhich of the above graphs shows a function with the period of \n1\n?\n\nMTue, Jul 29th @ 12:17 PM|Elapsed: 0:43\nCorrect\n3.Identifying the Period of a Function Given Its Graph\n?\n\nThe graph of a periodic function \n𝑦\n=\n𝑓\n(\n𝑥\n)\n is shown above. What is the period of this function?\n\nETue, Jul 29th @ 12:18 PM|Elapsed: 0:15\nCorrect",
